WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.912
A dashboard puts everything about a question on one page:

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:09.321
a scorecard per agent, a scorecard per queue, a trend by day, and

00:00:09.321 --> 00:00:11.246
the list of single calls.

00:00:11.246 --> 00:00:16.835
This video shows how the Report Builder makes one, with several queries, containers,

00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:19.940
and clicks that filter the rest of the page.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.060
A report groups its data one way.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.907
Totals per agent and a trend per day need two different groupings, so

00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:34.040
one query cannot show both.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:39.221
A dashboard gives each table or chart its own query, frames them in

00:00:39.221 --> 00:00:43.470
containers so the page stays tidy, and links them, so a click on

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.230
one filters the others.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.820
The person reading it asks the next question with a click:

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.660
which agent, which queue, which day, and then which calls.

00:00:57.843 --> 00:01:02.204
This is the Call dashboard, run from Reports, Report Builder.

00:01:02.204 --> 00:01:07.736
Four containers frame an agent scorecard, a queue scorecard, the calls per day,

00:01:07.736 --> 00:01:09.623
and the call selection.

00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:12.343
Click an agent in the scorecard.

00:01:12.343 --> 00:01:15.029
The other visuals show only that agent:

00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:17.536
the queues, the trend and the calls.

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.864
The picked row stays highlighted.

00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:23.874
Hold Control and click another agent to add them.

00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:27.174
Click Clear selection, and every row is back.

00:01:27.624 --> 00:01:31.310
Click a day on the chart, and the call selection narrows to the

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.592
calls of that day.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:36.172
Only the visuals a click is linked to load again; the rest of

00:01:36.172 --> 00:01:37.774
the page stays as it is.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.651
Choose Edit design.

00:01:43.651 --> 00:01:47.979
Under the tabs, the Query list holds the report's queries:

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:51.292
the main query, By queue, Calls and By day.

00:01:51.292 --> 00:01:54.200
Each has its own columns and filters.

00:01:54.652 --> 00:01:55.641
Pick By day.

00:01:55.641 --> 00:01:59.269
Its columns are the call date kept to the day, the number of

00:01:59.269 --> 00:02:01.358
calls and the average talk time.

00:02:01.358 --> 00:02:03.172
The chart shows this query.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:08.122
Add query makes a new query as a copy of the one you are editing.

00:02:08.122 --> 00:02:11.861
Give it a name, change its columns, and add a visual.

00:02:11.861 --> 00:02:15.093
Remove query takes it away, with its visuals.

00:02:19.294 --> 00:02:22.038
The Containers card lists the frames.

00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:25.674
Each shows its title and how many visuals it holds.

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:29.855
Add container asks for a Title, a Width and a Height.

00:02:29.855 --> 00:02:34.281
Pick Grow with its visuals for a frame as tall as what it holds.

00:02:34.281 --> 00:02:37.885
When the visuals are taller, they scroll inside it.

00:02:38.335 --> 00:02:42.214
A visual picks its frame in its own Container setting.

00:02:42.214 --> 00:02:46.545
Click the Agents table, and its Container is Agent scorecard.

00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:54.639
With the Agents table selected, look under When clicked.

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:58.155
Pick the value of says which column a click picks:

00:02:58.155 --> 00:02:59.286
here, Agent.

00:02:59.737 --> 00:03:02.811
Filter these visuals lists the other visuals.

00:03:02.811 --> 00:03:07.091
The Queues table, the Calls per day chart and the Calls table are

00:03:07.091 --> 00:03:10.467
checked, so a click on an agent filters all three.

00:03:10.918 --> 00:03:13.108
Select the Calls per day chart.

00:03:13.108 --> 00:03:16.719
It picks the Day, so a click on a day filters the Calls

00:03:16.719 --> 00:03:18.139
table to that day.

00:03:18.139 --> 00:03:21.218
A column that adds up values cannot be picked.

00:03:25.399 --> 00:03:28.861
Export keeps the containers where the format can.

00:03:28.861 --> 00:03:31.569
Excel and PDF are the two to look at.

00:03:33.169 --> 00:03:38.020
In Excel, each container is a worksheet named after it, with its visuals

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.005
one under the other, each under its title.

00:03:41.005 --> 00:03:45.359
Chart values are numbers, so you can chart or add them up there.

00:03:46.109 --> 00:03:50.935
In the PDF, a container's title is a band across the page, with

00:03:50.935 --> 00:03:52.823
its visuals under it.

00:03:52.823 --> 00:03:58.279
A CSV file has no sheets, so it lists the data of every visual in order.

00:04:02.479 --> 00:04:03.945
A service review:

00:04:03.945 --> 00:04:09.299
scorecards per agent and per queue, with the calls behind them one click away.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.521
A quality check:

00:04:11.521 --> 00:04:15.739
a trend by day, and a click on a bad day lists its calls.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.522
A hand-off to a manager:

00:04:18.522 --> 00:04:22.319
export to Excel, one worksheet for each container.

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:29.299
A Report Builder dashboard answers the first question and lets the reader ask

00:04:29.299 --> 00:04:31.219
the next one with a click.

00:04:31.219 --> 00:04:34.399
Queries, containers and links are all it takes.

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:35.959
Thanks for watching.

